1. PROPRIETARY OWNERSHIP
   All ZQX software components—including `zqx` (CLI), `zqxd` (node daemon),
   `zqx-tray` and `ZQX.app` (desktop clients), `zqxnode` (SDK), `zqx-core`,
   `zqx-proto`, `zqx-tunnel`, `zqx-ns`, `zqx-stir`, `zqx-control`
   (controller), `zqx-console`, and `zqx-saas`—and all related source code,
   object code, protocols, and documentation (collectively, the "Software"),
   except the Third-Party Components (Section 6), are the exclusive proprietary
   property of ZQX Net and its licensors.

2. LICENSE GRANT BY TIER
   Subject to compliance with this Agreement and applicable subscription payment,
   ZQX Net grants Customer a revocable, non-exclusive, non-transferable,
   non-sublicensable license to install and use the compiled binary Software
   solely according to Customer's active plan:

   (a) Personal Plan (Free):
       Free of charge for up to ten (10) users on the ZQX Hosted SaaS
       platform (`console.zqxnet.com`), with unlimited connected user devices.
       Does NOT include rights to operate self-hosted controllers.

   (b) Starter Plan (Per User):
       Billed per active user seat per month on the ZQX Hosted SaaS
       platform. Includes team SSO, granular ACL policies, and Fabric DNS. Does NOT
       include rights to operate self-hosted controllers.

   (c) Premium Plan (Per User):
       Billed per active user seat per month on the ZQX Hosted SaaS
       platform. Adds real-time SIEM audit export and cross-xnet sharing. Does NOT
       include rights to operate self-hosted controllers.

   (d) Enterprise Plan (Per User + Per Self-Hosted Controller):
       Billed per active user seat plus per licensed self-hosted controller
       instance (`max_controllers`). Grants the right to deploy and operate the
       compiled `zqx-control` and `zqx-console` binaries in sovereign, on-premises,
       VPC, or air-gapped environments up to the exact number of licensed
       controllers encoded in Customer's cryptographically signed `ZqxLicense`.
       Unlicensed local `zqx-control` instances may be used solely for internal
       non-production evaluation during the built-in 14-day evaluation period.

3. RESTRICTIONS
   Customer shall NOT (and shall not permit any third party to):
   (a) Copy, publish, disclose, or distribute any ZQX source code.
   (b) Reverse engineer, decompile, disassemble, or attempt to derive the source
       code or signing keys of the Software, except to the minimum extent
       expressly mandated by non-waivable applicable law.
   (c) Circumvent, tamper with, or bypass any `ZqxLicense` signature checks,
       user seat limits, controller count limits, or evaluation timers.
   (d) Host, resell, white-label, or offer the Software as a managed service or
       competing fabric controller service to third parties without written
       Enterprise MSP authorization from ZQX Net.

